# ============================================================
# AI-Setup .gitignore
# Git tracks the ARCHITECTURE (code, docs, curated chronicles).
# Volatile knowledge DATA (the live Store / learnings / session logs) is backed up
# separately by scripts/ops/snapshot_knowledge.py -- NOT committed (it churns constantly
# and would bloat history). See docs/BACKUP_AND_RECOVERY.md.
# ============================================================

# --- Private plane: personal assessments and operator-identifying material ---
# Daniil's ruling 2026-08-16: "Lets not commit the [REDACTED] and [REDACTED] stuff to the
# repo. I want to make sure its internally accesible." Locally readable by any seat, never
# pushed. (His words verbatim, two nouns bracketed -- naming the artifacts here would be the
# leak the rule exists to prevent, and a redacted quote keeps both the voice and the rule.)
# This is his private-plane directive (2026-08-15) in its smallest honest form: a PLACE with
# a procedure, not a redaction dance at the boundary. Anything about the operator as a
# person -- gradings, portraits, identifying detail -- lives here, not in the public tree.
private/

# --- Copyrighted design references (public repo -- assets stay LOCAL; the capture
#     is reproducible: scripts/capture_apple_hig.py + the OneUI URL in refs/design-inspiration docs;
#     only INDEX.md metadata is tracked) ---
refs/design-inspiration/oneui/
refs/design-inspiration/apple-hig/raw/
refs/design-inspiration/apple-hig/text/
refs/design-inspiration/apple-hig/images/

# --- Heavy third-party / generated trees (NOT our architecture) ---
ComfyUI-Zluda/
dockerized-ai/
backup_wsl_migration/
models/
assets/
session_screenshots/
build/
dist/
temp/
backups/
sessions/

# --- Virtualenvs / dependencies / caches ---
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.Python

# --- Volatile knowledge DATA (recover via scripts/ops/snapshot_knowledge.py) ---
session_logs/
blackboard_data/
coordinator_logs/
.pytest_out.txt
.pytest_err.txt
test_memory.json
test_data.json
test_code.json
*.jsonl
# test fixtures are CODE, not volatile data: exempt them from the jsonl blanket
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl
# the artifact-substrate durable record IS git-tracked by design (A1, T101):
# store/docs JSONL = the atoms' append-only ledger; git push = its off-machine backup
!store/docs/*.jsonl
# operator-ordered durable copies are records, not volatile data (Daniil 2026-08-11:
# "persist the entire transcript"): redacted session transcripts + reviewed research raws
!chronicles/transcripts/*.jsonl
!research/reviewed/**/*.jsonl
# corpus digests are the structured yield of a full-corpus sweep, not volatile output:
# they carry the typed edges (settles / contradicted-by / has-no-implementation / serves)
# that the rel: roster lacks, and re-deriving them costs a multi-agent read of ~1600 artifacts
!data/corpus-digests/*.jsonl
# auto-captured per-session draft (SessionEnd/PreCompact); ephemeral, regenerated each session
chronicles/last-session-draft.md

# --- Secrets (never commit) ---
.env
*.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets.*
credentials.*

# --- OS / IDE ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Binaries / archives ---
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.bin
*.exe

!.gitignore

# local secrets (API keys) -- never commit
.secrets/

# Bifrost media blobs (content-addressed, not source)
blobs/

# Bifrost session snapshots (runtime state; not source)
session_snapshots/

# Console file drops (runtime; shared into a session, not source)
dropbox/

# research-day runner: per-session stdout logs are scratch, not knowledge
research/drafts/*.session.log
research/drafts/*.session.log.err

# research/bakeoff outputs are bench artifacts until graded; only the report + promoted drafts ship
research/bakeoff/*/
!research/bakeoff/tasks/

# claude-fleet runtime scratch + session state (not source)
scratch/
state/*
research/runlog-*.md
research/shift-console-*.log
research/shift-console-*.log.err

# EXCEPTION: the coordination task-ledger is durable source-of-truth, not runtime scratch.
# state/* (not state/) excludes the CONTENTS so these re-includes can take effect.
!state/coord/
!state/coord/**
# EXCEPTION (2026-09-03): drill receipts are EVIDENCE, not scratch. House law says a
# recovery path without an executed-drill receipt is presumed broken -- and a receipt
# on an ignored path is invisible to every clone, so no clone can verify any drill
# (the drill_receipts_live_on_a_gitignored_path lesson, recurred tonight when a
# commit claimed a receipt that git had silently skipped).
!state/drills/
!state/drills/**

# EXCEPTION to the exception (t384): instance-bound, NOT durable source. This maps ONE
# Discord server's channel ids to seats; on a peer instance those ids address channels
# that do not exist, so pulled seat traffic routes into the void.
state/coord/discord_seat_channels.json

# EXCEPTION: the guardrail baseline is the RATCHET's memory, not runtime scratch (T178).
# Untracked, it was per-machine: every fresh clone and CI itself ran with no baseline, and
# ratchet_ok read a missing baseline as nothing-to-compare and PASSED. The debt allowance has
# to travel with the repo or "green" only ever means green on one workstation.
!state/ci/
state/ci/*
!state/ci/guardrail_baseline.json
research/sources-cache/
state/spill/

# Claude Code local settings never ship (CLI probe round-2 finding 2026-07-16)
.claude/settings.local.json
.kimi-claude-home/

# --- Library schema R12 (ratified 2026-07-21): play receipts are runtime; out/ is curated at wrap ---
data/play/*/runs/
# play thread transcripts are committed source per R12 (exemption from the jsonl blanket)
!data/play/**/threads/*.jsonl
# parked prehistory receipts are archive, not volatile data (exemption from the jsonl blanket)
!_archive/prehistory/*.jsonl
!store/docs/migration_map.json

# design inspiration (Apple HIG / Samsung OneUI) — LOCAL reference only, never on GitHub (Daniel ruling 2026-07-23)
refs/design-inspiration/

# UI screenshot evidence: regenerate with py scripts/ui_shot.py, never worth repo weight
artifacts/ui/*.png

# T158: canary answer keys must never enter a retrieval plane (lesson
# answer_keys_never_enter_retrieval_planes) -- untracked by rule, sha256 in the commit instead.
state/canary/
*.canary-key.json

# W156: which world this checkout IS. Untracked BY DESIGN -- the July 2026 sandbox put its
# isolation in tracked config.py and could therefore never be refreshed from prod without
# surrendering the isolation. See core/world.py.
.aurora-world

# W160: this checkout's restore points -- untracked for the same reason .aurora-world is.
.aurora-savepoints.json

# Session transcripts are NEVER committed to this repo (2026-08-15, Daniel's call).
# The repo is PUBLIC. The redaction approach that used to guard these copies was a
# retroactive denylist -- a race the leak wins: the 2026-08-11 pipeline ran 137 audited
# substitutions and reported "zero leaks", and a third party's surname survived it anyway
# on origin/master. Durability does not need this plane: scripts/ops/archive_transcripts.py
# already keeps UNREDACTED copies off-repo on two separate physical disks (E: and F:).
# Keeping them here duplicated that durability and added the only path by which it leaked.
chronicles/transcripts/*.jsonl
# the seats' faces ship with the repo -- raw.githubusercontent serves them as avatars
# (the assets/ ignore above predates this and guarded the dead AssetsManager download cache)
!assets/
!assets/avatars/
!assets/avatars/*.png

# INSTANCE-LOCAL AUTHORITY (t384). A grant minted on one Aurora instance must never apply
# on another: this file is per-machine truth, like .secrets/ and .claude/settings.local.json.
# Policy is NOT here -- role templates live in core/trust/capabilities.py::ROLE_TEMPLATES.
# Tracked template: security/acl.example.json. Ceremony: docs/DSH_INTEGRATION.md 8b.
security/acl.json
security/acl.json.bak*

# INSTANCE-LOCAL ROUTE (2026-08-24, found by Zadkiel on Serge's instance). A peer route is a
# fact about THIS machine's relationship to another, so committing it asserts one fleet's
# relationship as everyone's -- two correctly-configured Auroras will always disagree here,
# which makes a shared copy a guaranteed conflict rather than a risked one. Exactly the
# acl.json class (t384). Tracked template: state/coord/remote_bridge.example.json.
# Env override, no file edit needed: AKASHIC_REMOTE_BRIDGE_PEER_URL.
state/coord/remote_bridge.json
state/coord/remote_bridge_inbox.jsonl
state/coord/remote_bridge_outbox.jsonl

# Material authored by people outside the fleet is never tracked.
# Cite external work by reference; keep durable copies in private/correspondence/.
research/reviewed/*correspondence*
research/reviewed/outside-review-*

# Operator inner files off-tree by ruling (Daniil 2026-09-04, tier split / t384 pattern).
# The practice and its why ship publicly: charters/OPERATOR_GUIDE.md + the README stub.
charters/daniel/*
!charters/daniel/README.md
